    (DOC/'V0_6_9_TRACK_B_RESULTS.md').write_text('# v0.6.9 Track B result\n\nNo crop continuation was authorized because neither exact-element local baseline passed the complete measured-parent field gate. No contact setting, geometry, mesh, friction or material was changed. The selected correction is therefore none. The original pressure redistribution at 1.2675% is documented but not resolved.\n\nThe separate crop retains its v0.6.8 accepted maximum of **1.2575%**, full qualified restart at **1.2%**, native-converged but unqualified endpoint at **1.5%**, and 12 accepted curve points. No new 5%, 10%, 20%, 30% or 40% result exists. Repeated independent read-only POST1 exports of the accepted state agree byte-for-byte for 174,746 displacement nodes and 47,525 native corner stress/elastic-strain nodes, including SXX/SYY/SXY/SEQV and EXX/EYY/EXY. No midside stress values were fabricated.\n\nAt the accepted maximum, travel is 0.032192 mm, compressive force approximately 3.79009 N and nominal stress 1.48050 MPa. The accepted reaction imbalance remains 4.66e-9 and selected-pair endpoint penetration 9.6554e-7 mm. Internal general-contact pore skins remain open. No pore closure, buckling or collapse is established. Inherited curves and figures are explicitly labeled; diagnostic rejected histories are absent from accepted performance curves.\n\nE=1000 MPa, nu=0.3 and thickness1mm are provisional plane-stress elastic assumptions. This study cannot establish their physical suitability at 30–40% compression. Material tests covering finite compression, lateral deformation, unloading and relevant failure behavior are needed before selecting or calibrating a finite-strain constitutive law. No calibration data or new law was invented.\n',encoding='utf-8')
    (DOC/'V0_6_9_TRACK_A_STATUS.md').write_text('# v0.6.9 original full-specimen status\n\nThe Design9/seed1 original full specimen retains its independent accepted maximum of **0.9270608836206897%**, load step3/substep6. No full solve was launched, and source geometry, fine mesh, material and authenticated restart hashes remain unchanged.\n\nThe v0.6.8 expanded original-mesh local fixture imposed 15 full-parent cut histories but still failed its earliest three measured displacement/stress/strain comparisons, with roughly88% first-state SYY RMS error. Later displacement agreement near1e-6 does not repair this. Its measured near-zero-gap context also differs, despite balanced native local interface forces. Faces27837/27838/28504–28506 and nodes98184/99405/99399/4990 remain the verified hotspot.\n\nThe retained local evidence does not establish whether missing incremental stress/contact history, global compliance, cut traction or neighboring physical surfaces cause the early mismatch. This milestone focused the bounded native local work on Track B and did not silently transfer a crop correction to Track A. A parent-matched original local model with all early histories, traction/contact context and rigorous nanogap comparison remains necessary before any separately authorized full-model study.\n',encoding='utf-8')
    archives=sum(x['tests'] for x in tests['archives'])
    (DOC/'V0_6_9_VALIDATION.md').write_text(f'# v0.6.9 validation\n\nScientific status: **HOLD_LOCAL_PARENT_MATCH__NO_CROP_CONTINUATION**. Original full maximum0.9270608836%; separate crop maximum accepted1.2575%, inherited. Both local variants converged but fail onset stress/strain matching. No complete correction, full local gate or high-strain material validity is established.\n\nSoftware verification: {tests["active"]["tests"]} active tests; {archives} archived replay checks across {len(tests["archives"])} groups; {tests["licensed"]["tests"]} licensed-artifact checks, including12 new v0.6.9 checks. Categories overlap and are not summed. Scientific failed comparisons remain failed; passing evidence checks verify their preservation and gating.\n\nActual native work: {perf["native_process_count"]} native processes, {perf["source_solve_processes"]} local source solves, zero crop or full source solves. Summed native process wall time {perf["runtime_seconds"]:.3f}s; peak observed process-tree RSS {perf["peak_RSS_bytes"]/2**30:.3f}GiB; retained raw artifact usage {disk/2**30:.3f}GiB. These are sampled process measurements, not whole-system peak use. No resource cap stopped mechanics. The first read-only export was stopped for inefficient scalar queries.\n\nExact original element IDs, connectivity and quadratic midside geometry are retained. All measured histories are compared. Complete local gap/normal/reaction/continuous-intersection qualification remains unpassed, so no continuation is authorized. Final inherited fields were independently extracted twice and agree exactly. The source/mesh/native/restart bindings, two field comparison records, contact element histories, repeat extraction record and resource ledger are versioned under experiments/pipeline_v0.6.9/run_001. Historical protected source and results were not altered.\n',encoding='utf-8')
    answers=['No; the corner redistribution is diagnosed, but no correction passes the complete gate.','None.','No.','No; two onset states still fail even after expansion.','No.','1.2575% inherited crop; 0.9270608836% original full.','No.','No.','No.','No.','No.','No verified pore general-contact engagement; only the selected exterior pair is active at the accepted maximum.','No verified pore closure.','Yes in rejected historical crop states; none promoted to accepted performance.','Yes at the inherited accepted maximum; local equilibrium alone would not pass parent matching.','The 12-point inherited accepted curve is retained; no new curve points.','Yes; the inherited final native tensor fields were read twice with identical files.','No health limit stopped mechanics; one read-only job was stopped for inefficiency.','No.','Qualified continuous contact, full parent matching, material calibration and mechanical mesh sensitivity.']
